    "ai_summary": {
      "id": 752875,
      "summarized_text": "Shopify’s order-export CSV intentionally leaves many columns blank on rows after the first when an order contains multiple products. The first row contains order-level information, such as customer email, order status, totals, addresses, and shipping method; each additional row represents another line item and contains that item’s line-item data. The rows share the same order name/number, so blank cells indicate that the information applies to the order rather than being repeated for every product.\n\nFor analysis or packing workflows that require a complete order-level record on each row, the reply suggests filling those fields down only within rows with the same order number, using a helper formula. Line-item fields should not be filled down, and the modified CSV should not be re-imported into Shopify. The question was answered by explaining that the blank fields are expected behavior, not missing data.",
