  "comments": [
    {
      "author": "JWillumProducts",
      "text": "Yes, that’s by design. Shopify’s help page on exporting orders says that for orders with several line items, “additional line items” go on separate rows and “many of the fields are left blank to indicate that multiple items were purchased on the same order.” The first row carries the order-level data (email, statuses, totals, shipping/billing address, shipping method). The following rows carry only their own Lineitem columns. All rows share the same Name (order number). \n If you need every row filled, as in your Shopee data, fill the order-level columns down within the same order number only (helper column:  =IF(AND(C2=\"\",$A2=$A1),D1,C2) ). Don’t fill Lineitem columns. Don’t re-import the filled file into Shopify; use it for analysis or packing only.",
      "at": "2026-10-13T18:23:02.160Z",
      "url": "https://community.shopify.com/t/help-explain-the-data-fields-in-the-csv-file-when-exporting-an-order/336928/2"
    }
  ],
